6. TCP vs UDP--
            First understand: What is a packet?

            When you send data over the internet, it is broken into small pieces called packets.
           
            These packets travel through the internet and reach the destination.

    TCP--(Transmission Control Protocol)

        TCP is reliable.

        Before sending data, TCP checks:

        Is the receiver ready?
        Did all packets arrive?
        Did any packet get lost?
        Should I resend a lost packet?

            Where TCP is used
               --Banking
               --Website login
               --Email
               --File downloads
               --SSH (port 22)
               --HTTPS (port 443)

               --Because losing data here is unacceptable.

    UDP--UDP (User Datagram Protocol)

            UDP is fast.

            It does NOT check:

            Did packets arrive?
            Were packets lost?
            Should I resend?

            It just sends data.

            Where UDP is used
                ----Video calls
                ----Online gaming
                ----Live streaming
                ----DNS queries
                ----
                ----Because speed is more important than perfect delivery.

