8. Load Balancer = Traffic Police 🚦

               --Suppose:

               --10000 users

               --visit your website.

               --One server may crash.

               --So we use:

               --        Users
               --        |
               --    Load Balancer
               --    /   |   \
               --Server1 Server2 Server3

               --Load Balancer distributes traffic.

               --Benefits:

               --No server overload
               --Better performance
               --High availability

9. NAT Gateway

                    Imagine a private office.

                    Employees can go outside.

                    But outsiders cannot enter directly.

                    That's NAT.

                    AWS example:

                    Public Subnet
                        |
                    NAT Gateway
                        |
                    Private Subnet

                    Private servers can:

                    Download updates
                    Access internet

                    But internet cannot directly access them.
10. Routing = Road Map 🛣️

                    --When data travels, it needs directions.

                    --Example:

                    --Delhi → Jaipur → Jodhpur

                    --Similarly, routers decide:

                    --Computer A
                    --    ↓
                    --Router
                    --    ↓
                    --Internet
                    --    ↓
                    --Server

                    --Routing tells packets which path to follow.

                    --In AWS you'll see:

                    --Route Tables

                    --Example:

                    --0.0.0.0/0 → Internet Gateway

                    --Means:
                    
                    --"Send all internet traffic through the Internet Gateway."
